// Dialog :
"P2707083378" "It looks like Splice's device is working perfectly. Time to escalate this to the final plan."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1498186395" "So it all worked out? Good, that's the thing with robots. They're always reliable, they don't get chomped or slammed like <i>some</i> people around here.<br><br>Everything is about to go off without a hitch. Can you believe that? Something like this never happens.<br><br>Some of our undercover agents up top have gone forward to place the emitters on the ground. See, they look like just ordinary suitcases until I activate them - that's when they transform into a larger version of that emitter of yours to broadcast my signal.<br><br>It's going to be carnage on a massive scale, {HeroName}, and it's going to be <i>amazing</i>."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Splice 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro1 Text :
"P830109273" "<color orange>Santiago nods silently to you and holds up a makeshift computer screen. Splice is on it, smirking at you.</color><br><br>{HeroName}, finally. Let's get this party started.<br><br><color orange>Splice holds up a small television in the viewing screen, showing the area around the Magisterium. With a push of a button, a small wave of electricity is sent out. You see all the Clockwork in the area twitch for a moment before turning to attack the citizens around them. You notice Praetor White and Praetor Duncan are nowhere to be found.</color><br><br>It worked! Hah! I knew it! All this planning and it all came together!<br><br>I've been waiting months for this moment, {HeroName}. Remember <color yellow>Bravo Team trying to steal Marauder's day planner?</color><br><br>That was to make sure that <i>he</i> was scheduled to be somewhere else at this <i>exact moment</i>, just like Praetor Duncan. And Cole, from what I heard from our woman on the inside, is already off somewhere else.<br><br>And guess where the PPD are! Somewhere in the tunnels, thinking they've got a lead on where Calvin Scott is! And it was all orchestrated by ME!"
// Answer Text :
"P161136034" "Job well done. What's the next step?"
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P3866888114" "I've got a self-destruct device on the emitters. The signal should have spread through all of Nova, so now it's just a simple matter of destroying the evidence so they're none the wiser - hey! Hey! GET AWAY FROM THAT!<br><br><color orange>The screen shows several Clockwork tinkering with Splice's device. After a few moments, they turn and walk away. Splice furiously pushes a button on her handheld device.</color><br><br>It's not working. {HeroName}, it's not working! This is impossible, it's MY technology, it's supposed to work!<br><br>No, no no no no no! Those stupid Clockwork, why weren't they effected?!"
// Answer Text :
"P1284515333" "You sound like you have a problem."
// Page InformationPage2 Text :
"P3972881380" "We ALL do {HeroName}, if those emitters aren't destroyed, they'll be able to track it straight back to here, or worse, stop any future plans to do this in Imperial!<br><br>You're the only one who can go up there to destroy them - they'll just think you're a member of Powers Division, swooping in to save the day."
// Answer Text :
"P2925241926" "I'm on it. (Start Mission)"
// Answer Text :
"P279855379" "Give me a minute."
// Page Intro2 Text :
"P2177585590" "<color orange>Santiago points to an angry Splice on the screen.</color><br><br>Hurry, {HeroName}, the PPD won't be chasing a dead lead for long, and I'm sure Praetor White is on his way to the scene!"
// Answer Text :
"P4015148181" "I've got it covered. (Start Mission)"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P257159807" "Good news, {HeroName}, everything is all set to go. I normally don't say this, but I think you should get down here to watch the carnage with me. I have little devices planted on the emitters to monitor the situation.<br><br>You also shouldn't be around there when the carnage begins, it could be bad. {Hero.gender=male I'm actually growing a little fond of you, you're reliable.|I might care just a little bit if you get doused in fire.}<br><br>Meet up with our guy, Santiago. He's got a feed over to me. I wanna see your face when you hear the attack begin!"
// AcceptString :
"P72021100" "Alright, I'm on my way."
// SendOffString :
"P3434194450" "Great, just, you know, hurry up. We're on a schedule!"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P896216491" "Observe the Magisterium Carnage"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1232211416" "Come on! We've got a small window of opportunity here!"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P1664410901" "<color deepskyblue>Part Three: My Robot Butler, the Killer</color>"

